BT /F1 10 Tf 62 416 Td (- On the song page, show a chronological Hot 100 position timeline for the selected song.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 397 Td (- Provide a dark mode option and a shared 80s music montage background across all pages.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 54 378 Td (What The Application Does) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 354 Td (- The app presents an interactive view of Hot 100 chart activity from 1980 through 1989. It) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 340 Td (ranks songs by a success score that rewards both high chart placement and longevity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 321 Td (- The success score is calculated as the sum of 101 minus the Hot 100 position for every weekly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 307 Td (chart appearance. A number 1 week therefore contributes 100 points, while a number 100 week) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 293 Td (contributes 1 point.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 274 Td (- The main page visualizes the top 10 songs across the full decade.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 255 Td (- The year page filters rankings to a selected year and supports click-through song navigation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 236 Td (- The song page shows the selected song's week-by-week chart history with the y-axis reversed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 222 Td (so stronger chart positions appear higher on the chart.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 54 203 Td (Data And Database) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 179 Td (- The CSV file contains one row per song per chart week with these fields: chart_week,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 165 Td (current_week, title, performer, last_week, peak_pos, and wks_on_chart.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 146 Td (- load_hot100.py rebuilds the hot100 table from the CSV and derives the year column from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 132 Td (chart_week.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 113 Td (- The generated database contains indexes for year, song lookup, and chart week lookup to keep) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 99 Td (the Streamlit reports responsive.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62 80 Td (- The current loaded database has 52,200 chart rows covering years 1980 through 1989.) Tj ET
